From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_GPU_PASS_TIME=1 (log only): load census (common/nx2_load_census.h), one line group per 10 s: loads the OoT resource request thread issued (svc 0xF3 walks, [sp+0x108]), zstd one-shot decodes and stream starts by size + hash of the first 64 bytes, fs opens by path, file reads by name/offset/length, storage reads by offset/length; per source: events, MiB, distinct files, repeats within 60 s and the top 3 repeated; unset: as before

T180p (writer P), part 3 of EDEN_UP_GPU_PASS_TIME=1. Log only: which files the game loads, and
whether the steady loads in the area past the field are the same files again.
common/nx2_load_census.h: per source, events, MiB, distinct files, events whose file was seen less
than 60 s before ("seen again"), and the top 3 repeated files, one "EDEN_UP_LOAD_CENSUS" line per
source per 10 s (written by the thread with the first event after the 10 s). Sources:
- poll loads: the loads each walk of the OoT resource request thread issued ([sp+0x108] at svc
  0xF3; only with EDEN_UP_OOT_POLL_BACKOFF=1, where that svc exists); counts only, no names.
- zstd one-shot: ZSTD_decompressMultiFrame calls (svc 0xF0-0xF2, EDEN_UP_OOT_NATIVE_ZSTD=1), the
  file named by its compressed size and a hash of its first 64 bytes; MiB = output capacity.
- zstd streams: stream starts (svc 0xF4 in phase 1, EDEN_UP_OOT_ZSTD_STREAM=1), named by the first
  chunk's size and first 64 bytes (the frame header with content size and dictionary id).
- fs opens (IFileSystem::OpenFile, by path), fs file reads (IFile::Read, by the file's name,
  offset and length) and storage reads (IStorage::Read, by offset and length), any title.
Per event with the switch: a mutex, a hash map lookup and, for zstd, a 64-byte guest read; a name
string only the first time a file is seen; at most 32768 files per source, older than 60 s pruned
each line. Unset: one test of a static bool per event (and IFile keeps an empty string).
KEEPS THE STORE (no shader, pipeline or translation file).
